{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-langlands-dual","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-langlands-dual","kind":"definition","title":"$q$-Langlands dual group","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-gauge-group","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-su2"],"tags":["geometric-langlands","langlands-dual","quantum-group"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QLanglandsDual","text":"q-langlands-dual.md","leanSource":"q-langlands-dual.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:q-langlands-dual\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe with <a href=\"#def:quantum-gauge-group\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter\">quantum gauge group</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_q</code>. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Langlands dual group</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_q</code> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\check{G}_q = G_{q^{-1}}^{\\vee},</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(-)^\\vee</code> denotes the classical Langlands dual.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-langlands-dual.md","heading":"Definition","number":"24.4.1","page":"b/def-q-langlands-dual","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.QLanglandsDual","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-langlands-dual.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
